From ec40ebc214b512e822bb063aef13a36802834dc9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 20:13:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] lifecycle guard: `$(( $(date +%s) ... ))` is no
 shell sink

laptop-1 refused a read-only background watcher (`bash -n S && bash S`) with
"`~/.hermes/logs/hermes-sync.log` is larger than the scan cap ... a script the
command executes must be scannable". S only greps that log.

Repro (minimal): the refusal needs only S's
`deadline=$(( $(date +%s) + 2700 ))` plus two quoted reads of the over-cap log
(`grep "a" LOG` twice). Background mode, the `bash -n S && bash S` chain and the
pipe into tail/cut are not the trigger; the variable-path and foreground probes
passed because they lacked the arithmetic line.

Why: the command-position-substitution alternative of `_SHELL_SINK_RE` accepts
any `(` as a subshell opener, so the second paren of `$((` followed by
`$(date ...)` read as "a substitution whose output the shell runs". That
turned on the printed-payload walk, which treats every quoted literal and every
span between two quotes as a printed command; the span
`" LOG | tail ...\n grep -E "` put the log in command position, and the over-cap
log failed closed as an executed script.

Fix: exempt only the producer `$(date +%s)` (also '+%s'/"+%s"), whose output is
digits and so can run no command. The `(` anchor itself is unchanged: bash runs
code from other substitutions' output inside arithmetic, through array
subscripts (`x=$(( $(echo 'a[$(cmd)]') ))`) and through `((` falling back to
nested subshells (`(($(echo cmd)) )`) (review 5897778680 on an earlier head that
exempted every `$(` after `((`). The exemption is dropped when the command could
rebind `date`: a `date()`/`function date` definition, alias, hash, enable,
declare/typeset/export, PATH/BASH_ENV/ENV assignment, or source/`.` of a file.

Tests (tests/cron/test_lifecycle_guard_arith_sink.py, 64): the refused watcher
verbatim through the terminal guard (shared by background and foreground calls);
5 `$(date +%s)` arithmetic shapes x 4 data readers (grep, grep|tail|cut,
wc/sort, awk) inline and as `bash -n S && bash S`; the five reviewed shapes stay
sinks and still refuse an over-cap payload; other producers in arithmetic
(`$(y)`, `$(date +%F)`, `$(date)`, `$(date +%s; y)`) stay sinks; twelve rebind
prefixes stay sinks; executed files over the cap (bash/sh/source/./stdin/pipe)
still refuse. RED on origin/main: 26 failed. On earlier head 40277a28b8: 24
failed (the review regressions). GREEN here. tests/cron plus the guard
importers: 3028 passed, 9 skipped.

Residual, not changed here (pre-existing on main): a substitution after an
operator inside arithmetic (`x=$(( 1 + $(echo 'a[$(bash F)]') ))`) is no sink on
main either, since `+` is no command-position anchor. Follow-up card filed.
